{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqqu4akhnz5","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"production hole AST code edges extracted then dropped and search loop control is heuristic not LLM","summary":"Two-part production hole in the native code onboarding + agentic search, confirmed in code. PART 1 — structural wiring is computed then discarded: the AST extractor (lib/code-extract, babel + tree-sitter, all 7 langs) fully emits edges [{from,to,kind:'calls'|'imports',external?}] and index.js even resolves import specifiers to repo-relative paths, but lib/code-extract/ingest.js consumes ONLY symbols (-> code_nodes) and drops edges entirely (the lone reference is a comment at ingest.js:37 about '(later) edge sync' that was never built). These code-to-code edges are DETERMINISTIC ground truth (the code literally calls/imports) so they need NO judge — unlike cosine-guessed note-to-task autowire edges. The onboarder should persist them as code_node graph edges so round-1 DAG-gated retrieval can traverse code structure (callers/callees/imports) instead of relying on the cosine ranker. IMPLEMENTATION NUANCE: call edges are currently coarse (from=file, to=callee NAME, raw/unresolved — babel.js:50 'symbol-level resolution is a later phase'); import edges are resolved file->file. So Part 1 needs a symbol-resolution pass (callee name -> defining code_node) for true symbol-to-symbol wiring. PART 2 — the agentic search-loop controller should be an LLM, not heuristics: lib/subconscious/index.js makes ZERO model calls; chooseAgenticFollowup + agenticStopReason + the evidence_quality<0.18 gate are pure arithmetic. An LLM grader should sit BETWEEN rounds and own: (a) continue-or-stop, (b) next query reformulated from the original search intent + evidence so far, (c) keep/abstain per result (intent-aware relevance), (d) aggregate the final response to the searcher. Cost is O(rounds per search), bounded per search session — NOT the O(symbols x tasks) explosion that kept code out of the corpus-wide note edge-judge, so it is affordable. The heuristic ranker is demoted to a cheap prefilter feeding the LLM. Recommended sequencing: ship Part 1 first (deterministic, cheap, independently li","category":"project","tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T16:04:20.225Z","vec":[-0.11828137934207916,-0.01567106693983078,-0.053432390093803406,0.03495818376541138,0.026681572198867798,-0.06655466556549072,-0.02287408709526062,0.06468784809112549,0.02409248612821102,0.022509552538394928,0.002623202046379447,0.0010942707303911448,0.01905137673020363,-0.0485231950879097,-0.009410453960299492,0.05224219709634781,0.02331719547510147,0.004025710746645927,-0.05014561116695404,-0.0723467469215393,0.07803228497505188,-0.005105885211378336,-0.003043688600882888,-0.07216513156890869,-0.009862438775599003,-0.01875469833612442,-0.05635913461446762,-0.039134200662374496,0.023127514868974686,-0.06713472306728363,0.03193176910281181,0.12998974323272705,-0.01119948923587799,0.08331701904535294,0.006348039954900742,0.09217459708452225,-0.04926462471485138,-0.07837150990962982,-0.015223993919789791,-0.021766480058431625,-0.005364807788282633,0.11068204045295715,-0.03507493808865547,-0.061725035309791565,0.02271892875432968,-0.0329296737909317,-0.12595732510089874,-0.03193522244691849,-0.06849845498800278,-0.07630938291549683,-0.10484547168016434,0.013537831604480743,-0.0733327642083168,-0.06295394152402878,0.018792705610394478,0.029481906443834305,0.06239258497953415,-0.004418703727424145,-0.01245461031794548,-0.0076061743311584,0.06622940301895142,-0.017691517248749733,-0.011138920672237873,-0.04196269437670708,0.04583611711859703,-0.007341321557760239,-0.0178493894636631,-0.0005883365520276129,0.021152237430214882,0.009030335582792759,0.011746075004339218,-0.008890416473150253,-0.05768723785877228,0.02582985907793045,0.022257817909121513,0.02519947662949562,0.036651335656642914,0.07795171439647675,0.04775546118617058,-0.09398540109395981,-0.061117351055145264,-0.008353451266